{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "A free-pick Hero gets its Wrath ranks back as it levels after Prestige, never above its level (#10709)",
  "contract": [
    "Run on a free-pick realm (CoA.ClassModel = hero, CoA.RealmType = seasonal). Wrath is Character Advancement entry 40165 (spell 5176, rank 1); its higher ranks come from a class trainer along SpellRank.dbc: 5177 (level 6), 5178 (14), 5179 (22), 5180 (30), 6780 (38), 8905 (46), 9912 (54).",
    "Prestige drops every non-retained entry (AscensionFreepick::PrestigeSpecialization), and removing rank 1 removes the trained ranks, which AscensionWildcard remembers in core.wildcard.trainedranks. Re-learning rank 1 used to restore every remembered rank at once, whatever the level: a level 16 Hero held rank 7 (8905, level 46).",
    "After the fix a remembered rank comes back only when the character's level allows it, in ladder order: at level 16 ranks 2 and 3 are usable and rank 3 is the active one; ranks 4+ are not known; at level 22 rank 4 can be had again. trainer_buy is used for each rank so the scenario holds whether the rank is restored for free or bought again.",
    "Chromie only prestiges at the realm's level cap (CoAPrestige ResolveRequiredLevel = CONFIG_MAX_PLAYER_LEVEL; the gameplay env has MaxPlayerLevel = 80), so the Hero starts at level 80; below it Activate refuses with Refusal::BelowLevel and the level stays unchanged.",
    "Wrath ranks are SpellInfo::IsStackableWithRanks (mana power, not passive, not a form or aura), so learning a higher rank leaves the lower ranks known and active (Player::addSpell only deactivates non-stackable ranks); the scenario asserts that stock state rather than a superseded rank 1."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 180000,
  "players": [
    {
      "id": "hero",
      "name": "Prestiger",
      "race": 1,
      "class": 10,
      "level": 80,
      "security": 2
    }
  ],
